  "reasoning": "The defendants, as education officials, used their positions to illegally register non‑eligible candidates for the college entrance exam in exchange for money, which constitutes acceptance of bribes (受贿). Their actions also involved abusing public authority to manipulate the admission process, fitting the crime of abusing power for personal gain in student admissions (徇私舞弊罪). Additionally, they fabricated school and police seals and produced false academic and household certificates, which is the crime of forging state documents (伪造国家机关公文罪). Therefore, the appropriate charges are acceptance of bribes, abuse of power for personal gain in student admissions, and forging state documents.",
